  m_text: "Culinary History: An indigenous Filipino dish, Sinigang, also known as
    sour broth, due to the use of souring agents like tamarind, unripe mango and
    calamansi both for flavour and preservation in a hot humid climate. It\u2019s
    a common Filipino comfort food. Many variations exist and it is comprised of
    a mixture of a protein source, vegetables and something sour. "
